    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.07.168": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Advancement",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Advancement - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Administrative Assistant, Advancement University Relations Competition No. 26.07.168 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Non-Recurring Term (35 hours per week) MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). A review of applications will begin on August 5, 2026 and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Non-Recurring Term (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date A review of applications will begin on August 5, 2026 and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Administrative Assistant, Advancement for a full-time, 6-month non-recurring term opportunity with our University Relations department. You will provide comprehensive administrative, financial, and operational support to the Advancement portfolio. In this role, you will coordinate office operations, gift administration, meetings, recruitment activities, departmental projects, and advancement initiatives. You will also provide administrative support for donor stewardship, constituent record management, fundraising reporting, and advancement events while ensuring accuracy, confidentiality, and compliance with University policies and procedures. Key responsibilities include: Serving as the first point of contact for visitors, students, donors, alumni, and internal stakeholders by providing professional, courteous, and confidential customer service or redirecting requests to the appropriate staff member or department; Preparing, formatting, proofreading, and editing, correspondence, reports, presentations, proposals, gift agreements, and other documentation for review and approval while ensuring accuracy and adherence to university standards; Coordinating calendars, meetings and appointments for leadership and departmental staff; Assisting with planning departmental events, recognition activities and meetings, including preparing agendas and minutes, booking rooms and other logistics; Coordinating travel arrangements and travel expense documentation; Maintaining office supplies, promotional merchandise, equipment and coordinating repairs; Processing mail, courier requests, parking pass administration and other departmental memberships and professional association renewals; Assisting with SharePoint administration, records organization and document management; Processing cheque, cash, e-transfer, wire transfer, and Gift-in-Kind donation documentation in accordance with established procedures; Preparing and reconciling purchase requisitions, invoices, P-Card transactions and expense documentation; Maintaining and tracking records of stewardship activities, constituent and donor records in Raiser's Edge and updating Raiser's Edge in accordance with established procedures; Managing the Advancement shared email inboxes and voicemail, responding to routine inquiries and directing requests to the appropriate staff member; Providing administrative support for donor stewardship activities, alumni engagement initiatives, MMB tours, fundraising campaigns, annual giving initiatives and other related activities; and Assisting with recruitment activities including posting support, interview scheduling, candidate communications, onboarding and offboarding activities and payroll/human resource documentation. Skills You will have: Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines; Strong attention to detail and accuracy in preparing documentation, maintaining records, and processing financial and donor information; Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills with a strong customer service orientation; The ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with donors, alumni, senior leaders, and internal stakeholders; The ability to exercise sound judgment, discretion, and confidentiality when handling sensitive information; Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to identify issues and implement appropriate solutions; The ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment; Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and the ability to learn and utilize systems such as Raiser's Edge, PeopleSoft, and SharePoint; Strong administrative and coordination skills, including meeting and event coordination, records management, recruitment support, and financial administration; and The initiative, adaptability, and the ability to respond effectively to changing priorities in a fast-paced environment. Qualifications A minimum of a 2-year post-secondary diploma in business administration, office administration, administrative professional, public administration, or a related field. Minimum 3 years of progressively responsible administrative experience supporting senior leaders or complex business operations, Experience with financial administration, recruitment coordination, records management, event coordination, and confidential administrative support. Experience supporting advancement, alumni relations, donor administration, or a comparable customer relationship management environment would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.204": {
      "title": "Admissions Assistant",
      "description": "Admissions Assistant - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Admissions Assistant Office of the University Registrar Competition No. 26.08.204 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 17, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 17, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Admissions Assistant for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Office of the University Registrar. The position is an integral member of the Admissions team and is accountable for providing exemplary service, preparing admission files for evaluation, and providing support to the admission team. You will receive, organize, and manage related information and documentation to prepare a file for admission evaluation. Additionally, you will respond to future students, applicants, and parents regarding a broad range of inquiries related to applicant file status, admissions and transfer policies, procedures, and documentation requirements. Key responsibilities include: Entering applications and supporting documents (i.e. transcripts, test scores) into the student information system; Identifying and confirming receipt of academic transcripts and related admission documentation required for the evaluation of applications, and, where required, scanning and uploading to the electronic document management system and student record; Reviewing academic transcripts and applicable admission documents to verify authenticity and completeness, using multiple resources; Providing accurate admission information to future students, applicants, parents, and stakeholders by email or other electronic communication tools; Assisting applicants in understanding their admission and transfer credit statuses; Engaging with the Admissions team to ensure accurate and consistent information is provided to applicants, students, and staff; Identifying and recommending new or revised procedures where efficiencies can be optimized; and Assisting with and supporting the collaborative training model for new and existing employees. Skills You will have: Excellent written and verbal communication skills; A service-oriented approach with the ability to serve diverse prospective students, applicants, and other stakeholders with empathy, professionalism, clarity, consistency and conciseness; The ability to perform intermediate-level tasks using a student information system; Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), SharePoint, Google and other software applications; The ability to organize time and priorities with limited supervision to meet goals and objectives; The ability to understand and anticipate applicants need using critical thinking and problem-solving skills; The ability to process large volumes of work and meet deadlines; Aptitude for accuracy and thoroughness with keen attention to detail; The ability to demonstrate flexibility and adaptability in a dynamic environment; and The ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Qualifications A minimum of a Diploma (two-year) with a focus on records/data management, administration or related areas. A minimum of one (1) year of administrative support and/or data management experience in program evaluation settings. Experience in a post-secondary institution in an administrative setting would be considered an asset. Knowledge of PeopleSoft - Campus Solutions would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.194": {
      "title": "Aquatics Programmer",
      "description": "Aquatics Programmer - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Aquatics Programmer Sport and Wellness Competition No. 26.08.194 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 8, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 8, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Aquatics Programmer for a full-time continuing opportunity with our Sport and Wellness department. Reporting to the Supervisor, Aquatics, you will be responsible for developing, coordinating, promoting, implementing and evaluating aquatic programs and initiatives that foster a sense of community, promote physical well-being and support the diverse needs of our students, faculty and staff. You will also deliver a range of engaging activities and events that enhance the overall campus experience. Key responsibilities include: Developing, planning and coordinating a variety of aquatic programs that engage students, faculty, staff, and external community members; Ensuring that programs meet or exceed the standards of the Lifesaving society and regulatory safety standards while aligning with broader Sport and Wellness departmental strategies and goals; Developing and maintaining a comprehensive calendar and coordinating the scheduling for aquatic programming to ensure efficient allocation of pool time between institutional programs, recreational use, external bookings, seasonal programs and special campus events; Preparing detailed lesson plans, activity outlines, and contingency plans to ensure smooth execution of programs; Monitoring and assessing program participation and outcomes, collecting feedback to inform program improvements and to ensure continuous enhancement; Adapting programming to suit the facility’s usage patterns, including peak hours and facility availability as well as aligning scheduling with the availability of trained staff; Engaging with academic departments and external stakeholders to promote Sport and Wellness programs and services; Maintaining inventory of aquatic supplies; Monitoring external bookings and collection of fees; Acting as the primary point of contact for external groups, providing excellent customer service and clear communication regarding availability, policies, and pricing; Conducting routine audits of programming and staffing to verify compliance with ratios and certification requirements; Providing program delivery supports for First Aid and Fit testing, incident reporting, hazard assessments, respiratory protection, and PPE programs; and Serving as a backup to the Head Lifeguard/Instructor when necessary, assisting staff with issues that arise during day-to-day operations of the pool. Skills You will have: Strong knowledge of aquatic programming and principles, practices and techniques employed in water safety and lifesaving activities; Excellent organizational and time management skills, with keen attention to detail; Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communications skills with the ability to work with a diverse range of clients and colleagues; Strong problem-solving skills with the ability to respond professionally under pressure; Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite; and The ability to remain flexible, take initiative and work both independently and in a team environment. Qualifications A minimum of a diploma in Recreation, Sports Management or related field. A minimum of 2 years of experience in aquatics programming and instruction or a similar role, preferably in a post-secondary or community setting. Certified in Lifesaving National Lifeguard (NL), Lifesaving Society Swim and Lifesaving Instructor, Intermediate First Aid with CPR-C and Automated External Defibrillator (AED), and Lifesaving Society Oxygen Administration, with the ability to renew annually or as required. Certification in First Aid Instructor, National Lifeguard Instructor, AARFP Pool Operator 1 and level 2 are all considered assets. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. The ability to work flexible work hours, including shift work, rotating schedules, evenings and weekends. The successful incumbent will be required to obtain a Police Record Check with a Vulnerable Sector Check at their own cost. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.179": {
      "title": "Case Manager",
      "description": "Case Manager - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Case Manager Office of Student Support and Accountability Competition No. 26.08.179 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 8, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 8, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking Case Managers for 2 full-time continuing opportunities with our Office of Student Support and Accountability. In this role, you will provide non-clinical case management for students experiencing complex personal, medical, mental health, behavioural, safety-related, or wellness concerns. As a core member of the Collaborative Assessment, Response, and Evaluation (CARE) Team, you will contribute to case analysis, risk-informed recommendations, and guidance on coordinated responses for students of concern. Although this is a non-clinical role, it requires strong knowledge of mental health, behavioural risk, trauma-informed practice, crisis response, privacy, and student support systems. The position uses professional judgment to support students in distress and help the University respond to situations that may affect student well-being or campus safety. The role may also provide on-call support outside normal working hours for urgent or complex student matters that require timely follow-up, coordination, or escalation. Key responsibilities include: Conducting intake, triage, and psychosocial assessments for students experiencing complex non-academic concerns, including acute mental health crises, and/or behavioral health concerns, risk of harm to self or others, violence risk, trauma related concerns or other barriers that may affect well-being, functioning or safety, including but not limited to housing stability and food security; Assessing student needs, level of concern, urgency, and potential risk to self or others using evidence-informed tools, established protocols, and structured professional judgment; Applying trauma-informed, equity-centered, culturally responsive, and strengths-based approaches when assessing student circumstances and determining appropriate support pathways; Providing consultation and direct case management support to students, faculty, staff, and service partners, including navigating university services, community resources, emergency supports, and ongoing care options; Maintaining accurate, detailed, and professionally sound case documentation, including assessment findings, care plans, risk assessments, intervention rationale, referrals, follow-up, and key case decisions, to support continuity of care, accountability, and legally defensible records; Coordinating access to internal university support services and external community supports; Assisting with transition and return-to-campus planning, including consideration of behavioural expectations, functional readiness, and available supports, when determined appropriate; Contributing to the development of case management protocols, referral pathways, documentation standards, care planning templates, and response protocols; Identifying trends, emerging issues, service gaps, and recurring risk factors from case work to inform program, policy, or process improvements; and Ensuring case management practices align with privacy legislation, institutional policies, professional standards, trauma-informed practice, and current best practices. Skills You will have: Advanced knowledge of mental health, behavioural risk, crisis response, trauma-informed practice, suicide risk, threat assessment concepts, and student support systems; Strong ability to conduct psychosocial assessment, risk triage, structured professional judgment, intervention planning, and case prioritization; Knowledge of privacy legislation, informed consent, confidentiality, duty of care, procedural fairness, and institutional risk considerations in a post-secondary environment; Strong consultation skills, including the ability to guide faculty, staff, and administrators through complex student situations with professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment; The ability to coordinate multi-disciplinary responses involving students, academic units, student services, security, counselling, accessibility services, residence, conduct, external providers, and emergency services; Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate sensitive information clearly, respectfully, and appropriately to diverse audiences; The ability to remain calm, organized, and responsive in crisis or high-pressure situations; Strong documentation skills, including the ability to record relevant case information, assessment rationale, intervention plans, and decisions accurately and professionally; A commitment to accessibility, cultural safety, and student-centered practice; The ability to identify trends, service gaps, and systemic barriers and contribute to continuous improvement in student support processes; and A commitment to ongoing professional development and maintaining current knowledge of trends, evidence-informed practices, professional standards, and emerging issues in student case management, mental health, behavioural intervention, risk assessment, and post-secondary student support. Qualifications A minimum of a Master’s degree in social work, counselling psychology, psychology, psychiatric nursing, clinical psychology, or a related mental health, counselling, or human services field. A minimum of 5 years of related experience in complex case management, mental health, crisis response, counselling, social work, behavioural intervention, student affairs, health care, community services, or a related field. Experience in a post-secondary environment would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. This position may be required to provide on-call support outside normal working hours to maintain continuity of support for urgent, complex, or time-sensitive student situations. After-hours support may involve consultation, coordination, referral, escalation, or follow-up in accordance with established protocols. The successful incumbent will be required to obtain a Police Record Check with a Vulnerable Sector Check at their own cost. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.198": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Executive Assistant - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Executive Assistant Office of the President Competition No. 26.08.198 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) $67,936 to $91,714 per annum September 7, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary $67,936 to $91,714 per annum Closing Date September 7, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Executive Assistant, Office of the President for a full-time continuing opportunity. Reporting to the Chief of Staff, the Executive Assistant provides senior-level administrative and operational support to the President and Vice-Chancellor and the Office of the President. You will serve as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders, managing complex calendars, communications, travel, and office operations. You will also support the coordination of priorities, initiatives, and events, while exercising a high degree of professionalism, political acumen, discretion, and sound judgment. Key responsibilities include: Serving as the first point of contact for the Office of the President by evaluating, redirecting, or responding to requests which includes researching information and providing appropriate responses; Managing the dynamic and complex schedule and calendar of the President and Vice-Chancellor, ensuring meetings, events, and other activities and appropriately prioritized; Managing correspondence for the Office of the President by reviewing and prioritizing incoming communications, drafting and preparing materials for the President and Vice-Chancellor’s speaking and meeting engagements, routine communications and standard correspondence; Coordinating logistics for travel, conferences, and meetings for the President and Vice-Chancellor, ensuring efficient itineraries and the best use of their time; Supporting the preparation of weekly Executive Council meetings and bi-weekly Dean’s Council meetings by coordinating meeting attendees, assisting with agenda preparation and compiling meeting materials; Contributing to the development, implementation, and ongoing improvement of administrative systems, processes, and protocols within the Office of the President; Ensuring the delivery of high-quality, professional documentation through advanced editing, formatting, and quality assurance practices; Overseeing daily office operations, identifying opportunities to enhance efficiency, service delivery, and stakeholder experience; Developing and maintaining robust records management systems to ensure effective information governance, accessibility, and compliance; Preparing reports, dashboards, tracking tools and expenditure disclosure to support operational oversight and decision-making; Exercising financial stewardship by reconciling procurement card transactions, reviewing expense claims, and ensuring compliance with institutional policies; Managing vendor relationships and procurement processes, including sourcing, quoting, and coordination with internal and external partners; Collaborating with the Chief of Staff in planning, coordinating, and executing a wide range of events for the Office of the President, ensuring seamless delivery and alignment with institutional priorities; and Assisting with event planning, logistics, and preparation of high-profile campus events in consultation with the Chief of Staff and University Relations. Skills You will have: Advanced organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple competing priorities in a fast-paced environment; Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to draft, edit, and proofread professional correspondence and reports; Sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to handle highly confidential and sensitive information; High attention to detail and accuracy in all aspects of work, including scheduling, documentation, and reporting; Proficiency in office software and digital tools such as Microsoft Office Suite, calendar management systems and collaboration platforms; Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to interact effectively and professionally with diverse internal and external stakeholders; Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills, with the ability to anticipate needs and respond proactively; and The ability to adapt to changing priorities and exercise flexibility in a dynamic executive office environment. Qualifications A minimum of a diploma in business administration, office administration, communications, or a related field. A minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible administrative experience. A minimum of 2 years of experience supporting an executive. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Out of Scope employee policy (D1015). Applications sourced through this process may be considered for similar opportunities within MacEwan University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.205": {
      "title": "Finance and Accounting Technician",
      "description": "Finance and Accounting Technician - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Finance and Accounting Technician Academic Affairs, Faculties of Health and Community Studies and Nursing Competition No. 26.08.205 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). October 9, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date October 9, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Finance and Accounting Technician for a full-time continuing position within Academic Affairs. Reporting to the Finance Officer, you will provide a range of support services to your portfolio of clients, ensuring their financial needs are met through tracking, reporting, reconciling financial reporting information, administering project grants, and assisting with other processes as needed. This position portfolio includes the Faculty of Health and Community Studies as well as the Faculty of Nursing. Key responsibilities include: Performing reconciliation of financial information and preparing journal entries; Preparing reports, pivot tables, and tracking sheets; Assisting with operating and capital budgets preparation; Answering finance-related staff and vendor inquiries; Following financial processes and statements to ensure compliance with professional accounting standards, contractual, legislative obligations, and organizational financial reporting requirements; Reviewing and tracking various financial accounting procedures and workflows to ensure that potential problems or concerns are addressed immediately; Preparing and ensuring the accuracy and timely submission of various transactions including fund transfers, journal entries, invoices, and purchase requisitions; Preparing and reviewing reports with budget holders, monitoring budgets and account balances and investigating discrepancies; Performing initial report analysis to support various financial management systems; Documenting processes that support efficient transaction flow, appropriate internal control, and compliance with university financial policies, procedures, and timelines; Reviewing capital asset requirements with programs and assisting with procurement and management of assets; Participating in asset counting where needed and reviewing asset records for accuracy, actioning asset transfers or disposal as needed; and, Other duties as assigned. Skills You will have: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with a keen attention to detail; Excellent verbal and written communication skills, for effective communication in writing, in person, and during presentations; Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to adapt to changing priorities with tight deadlines; The ability to work independently as well as within a broader team; Knowledge of accounting principles and financial reporting; Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and in data analytics; and, The ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise discretion, and tact. Qualifications A minimum of a diploma in Finance, Accounting, or related discipline. A minimum of 3 years of related experience. Experience processing a variety of financial transactions. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.185": {
      "title": "Finance Business Solutions Analyst",
      "description": "Finance Business Solutions Analyst - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Finance Business Solutions Analyst Shared Services Centre, Financial Services Competition No. 26.08.185 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band F (Steps 1-8): $36.722 - $53.420 per hour. $66,833 - $97,225 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week) September 6, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band F (Steps 1-8): $36.722 - $53.420 per hour. $66,833 - $97,225 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week) Closing Date September 6, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Finance Business Solutions Analyst for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Shared Services Centre of the Financial Services department. This is an exciting opportunity to work in a collaborative and service-focused environment where your expertise will directly contribute to the success of MacEwan’s University community. As a Finance Business Solutions Analyst, you will report to the Team Lead, Business Solutions and support the operation and optimization of our financial and procurement processes and systems, aligning with institutional priorities and MacEwan’s Teaching Greatness Strategic Vision 2030. You will be responsible for analyzing, recommending, and leading business solution activity and playing a pivotal role in influencing positive change. If you are keen, motivated and eager to learn, we encourage you to apply today! Key responsibilities include: Optimizing and maintaining systems and reporting Anticipating, engaging, and collaborating with business partners to solicit and analyze data for business requirements, in order to design and recommend optimal solutions; Maintaining system configurations and developing queries to meet the needs of clients by supporting business reporting objectives; and Providing expertise, analysis, and recommendations on internal financial system controls, steering system enhancements and/or new functionality to better serve end users, while ensuring effective risk management within system security administration and configuration controls; Maximizing solution-based analysis and supporting data integrity Conducting data analyses using various tools and methodologies to identify gaps between business requirements and system functionality, providing optimal solutions to all stakeholders; Developing business process risk assessments and treatment solution plans; Analyzing and report on data trends; and Contributing to and support strategic decision making by providing relevant data. Empowering innovative thinking and proactively addressing opportunities within system and business processes Applying analytical thinking, business knowledge, and subject matter expertise to address key business needs, issues, and pain points, then proactively seeking and facilitating solutions with key stakeholders; Benchmarking best practices and continually reviewing business processes and workflows for improvement opportunities; and Supporting the development and implementation of new systems, functionality, and processes. Being a change agent Providing leadership and expert advice to end users through communication and training, to promote continuous process improvement; Utilizing a business analysis lens to introduce and manage change for new system functionality and business operational changes; and Acting as a change leader within the Financial Services team, while building strong business partnerships and promoting the Shared Services Centre. Foster a culture of collaboration with stakeholders across the University Building strong business partnerships to solicit and document business requirements, share knowledge expertise, bridge technology business solutions, train on delivered solutions, or recommend business solutions; Facilitating meetings or workshops with stakeholders to gather and validate requirements, as well as developing and delivering presentations to communicate findings and recommendations; and Participating in departmental planning initiatives to develop objectives and action plans as required. Skills You will have: Strong analytical and investigative skills with an aptitude for problem solving; A critical thinking skillset and exercise design-minded strategies to evaluate processes, troubleshoot issues, and recommend effective solutions; Exceptional elicitation and comprehension skills for business requirement gathering; Excellent verbal and written communication, interpersonal, and facilitation skills; Strong attention to detail and initiative to maintain accurate and thorough quality work; The ability to maintain confidentiality while working with sensitive information; A collaborative mindset with the ability to build strong working relationships with a dynamic set of stakeholders across administrative and academic departments; High motivation to work effectively in a collaborative and fast-paced team environment as well as independently; Strong time management and organizational abilities to balance competing priorities and adaptability to meet deadlines; and Thorough understanding of change management best practices. Qualifications A minimum of a bachelor’s degree in business administration, information technology, or a related field from a recognized post-secondary institution. A minimum of 4 years of progressive business analysis work experience, including at least 2 years supporting multiple functional areas (eg. Finance, procurement, contract management) within a medium-to-large organization A minimum of 5 years of experience in working with a multi-faceted ERP system. Working knowledge of PeopleSoft Finance and Supply Chain Management system is preferred, or another ERP solution combined with directly relevant on-the-job experience. A certificate in business analysis or business process management would be considered an asset. A certificate in Change Management would be considered an asset. A background in working in a post-secondary institution with demonstrated knowledge of industry best practices and business processes would be considered an asset. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook and Visio) as well as the ability to adapt to new software products quickly and effectively. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Association Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.07.162": {
      "title": "Game Day Production Staff",
      "description": "Game Day Production Staff - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Game Day Production Staff Griffins Athletics Competition No. 26.07.162 Category Salary Closing Date Casual (less than 35 hours per week) MSU Band A (Steps 1-8): $16.845 - $24.515 per hour. September 4, 2026 Category Casual (less than 35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band A (Steps 1-8): $16.845 - $24.515 per hour. Closing Date September 4, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University Griffins Athletics is seeking to fill multiple Game Day Production Staff positions covering soccer, hockey, volleyball, and basketball game days running from September to March. All positions are casual part time and require evening and weekend work. This role is ideal for students interested in sports media, journalism, or broadcasting with a passion for sports and knowledge of soccer, hockey, volleyball, and basketball. We are looking for individuals who are outgoing team players with a keen interest in learning about sports and production. If you have an interest in behind-the-scenes productions and want to help provide an engaging game day experience for the fans, we want to hear from you! By applying to this job posting, there will be the potential to be trained and/or work all of the following positions: Camera Operator Setting up and tearing down all camera equipment and troubleshooting as required. Delivering high-quality footage for Canada West TV streams and in-game video board. Capturing live action footage that aligns with broadcast standards, including tight tracking of gameplay, smooth transitions, and dynamic framing of key moments like attacks, blocks, three-pointers, goals, and celebrations. Stream Operator Overseeing the production of MacEwan Griffins home games on Canada West TV. Setting up and tearing down production equipment and completing sound/video checks; troubleshooting as required. Communicating with camera operators and commentators, directing camera operators and on-air talent, and following the provided script to ensuring that every stream meets the quality expectations set by the MacEwan Griffins and Canada West. Video Board/ Replay Operator (Volleyball & Basketball Only) Setting up and tearing down production equipment and completing sound/video checks; troubleshooting as required. Overseeing all game replays to be played back on Canada West TV streams and on the in-gym video board, as well as operator the in-gym video board. Communicating with camera operators and in-game public address announcers, following the provided script to ensuring that every game meets the quality expectations set by the MacEwan Griffins and Canada West. Play-by-Play/Colour Commentator: Delivering live, real-time narration of the match, including calling the action point by point, providing team context, and highlighting key performances to provide a professional and entertaining broadcast experience. Setting up and tearing down broadcast equipment, conducting pre-game audio tests, researching player stats and game storylines ahead of each game, memorizing home team rosters including names, numbers, and faces, and following the provided script to ensuring that every game meets the quality expectations set by the MacEwan Griffins and Canada West. Public Address Announcer: Creating an engaging and exciting atmosphere for fans by delivering clear, enthusiastic live announcements and playing music throughout the game. Introducing starting lineups, announces goals, baskets, substitutions, fouls, timeouts, penalties, and more. Providing important event information such as sponsor messages, halftime promotions, and safety protocols. Setting up and tearing down broadcast equipment, conducting pregame audio tests, memorizing home team rosters including names, numbers, and faces, and following the provided script to ensuring that every game meets the quality expectations set by the MacEwan Griffins and Canada West. Skills You will have: Excellent time management and punctuality; Strong focus and attention to detail; and Working knowledge of soccer, hockey, volleyball, and basketball. Qualifications A minimum of a high school diploma. Experience in live broadcast production would be considered an asset. All skill levels are welcome, and on-the-job training can be provided. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. The ability to work all shifts between Thursday to Sunday afternoons and evenings. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply Please include in your cover letter which game day position(s) you are interested in working or being trained to work. To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
