      "title": "Mascot Performer",
      "description": "Mascot Performer - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Mascot Performer Griffins Athletics Competition No. 26.07.173 Category Salary Closing Date Casual (less than 35 hours per week) MSU Band A (Steps 1-8): $16.845 - $24.515 per hour. September 4, 2026 Category Casual (less than 35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band A (Steps 1-8): $16.845 - $24.515 per hour. Closing Date September 4, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University Griffins Athletics is seeking a Mascot Performer to wear the Griff the Griffin mascot costume at MacEwan Griffins home games and university events. This opportunity runs from September to March as a casual part time position and requires evening and weekend work. This opportunity is ideal for individuals who are outgoing, energetic, and love to put on a show in front of hundreds of fans and want to help create school spirit around MacEwan! Key responsibilities include: Performing as Griff the Griffin and embodying the character during MacEwan Griffins home games, community events, and university appearances; Engaging with all Griffins fans and MacEwan students attending games by taking pictures with fans and/or handing out swag in stands; Entertaining fans at home games with sideline antics and crowd engaging chants; and Participating in in-game contests and/or skits. Skills You will have: Excellent time management and punctuality; Outgoing personality with the ability to work well in a team environment; and Clear communication. Qualifications A minimum of a high school diploma. Experience in mascot performing would be considered an asset. Knowledge of soccer, volleyball, basketball, and hockey would be considered an asset. All skill levels are welcome, and on-the-job training can be provided. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. The ability to work all shifts between Thursday to Sunday afternoons and evenings. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.184": {
      "title": "Peer Academic Support Assistant (Student Casual)",
      "description": "Peer Academic Support Assistant (Student Casual) - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Peer Academic Support Assistant (Student Casual) MacEwan Academic Advising Centre, Office of Student Experience and Development Competition No. 26.08.184 Category Salary Closing Date Student Casual (less than 35 hours per week) MSU Band A (Steps 1-8): $16.845 - $24.515 per hour. A review of applications will begin August 20, 2026, and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Student Casual (less than 35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band A (Steps 1-8): $16.845 - $24.515 per hour. Closing Date A review of applications will begin August 20, 2026, and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking Peer Academic Support Assistants for 2 casual opportunities with our MacEwan Academic Advising Centre. You will provide front-line, peer-based information and navigation support to assist students with their university transition and encourage early engagement with academic advising supports. By sharing general information already documented in approved university materials, the role helps peers understand and navigate academic advising resources, basic institutional processes, and foundational academic information. Through these peer-to-peer interactions, the role helps students locate and understand the resources they need and guides them toward appropriate advising and support services. The role functions strictly as an information and referral resource and does not interpret policy, apply information to individual student circumstances, recommend academic decisions or pathways, or provide case-specific advising. All complex, individualized, or policy-related matters are referred directly to an Academic Advisor. This role enhances access to advising information through a relatable peer perspective, while complementing the existing Academic Advising ecosystem. Key responsibilities include: Providing peer-to-peer academic information and navigation support through drop-in services and live chat, limited to general information, processes, and approved resources; Responding to general inquiries by providing a general understanding of programs of study and requirements; Providing general information drawn from approved university resources, including websites, brochures, handouts, and published advising materials, and helping students locate and understand those resources at a general level; Referring students to an Academic Advisor within MacEwan Academic Advising Centre or Faculty/School-based Academic Advisor when inquiries require individualized interpretation, academic judgment, policy application to a specific situation, course planning, enrolment decision making, or case-specific guidance; Supporting students in booking appointments with appropriate advising units when needed; Sharing relatable peer perspectives and insights on the student experience, including effective strategies for navigating university life and academic expectations while maintaining appropriate role boundaries; Promoting awareness and understanding of Academic Advising services at MacEwan, acting as a student ambassador by encouraging early and proactive engagement with advising and institutional supports; and Delivering small group sessions and workshops focused on foundational academic navigation topics. Skills You will have: A foundational understanding of university structures, academic policies, program requirements, and advising resources, with the ability to navigate institutional systems to locate accurate information; Strong information-seeking and problem-solving skills, including the ability to identify appropriate sources and verify information before responding; Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage peers in an approachable and supportive way; Active listening skills to clarify student questions and respond appropriately to diverse needs; Customer service orientation with sound judgment and professionalism; The ability to maintain appropriate role boundaries, recognize scope limitations, and refer students to Academic Advisors or other services when necessary; The ability to locate, understand, and communicate general institutional information clearly, concisely, and in student-friendly language using approved resources and messaging; Proficiency using digital platforms and tools; and Basic facilitation and presentation skills for small group sessions. Qualifications Must be currently enrolled as an undergraduate student with a minimum of 90 credits completed. A minimum cumulative 3.0 GPA with good academic standing and no history of academic misconduct. Experience in a customer-facing, peer support, student service, volunteer, or leadership role that involves direct interaction with students, customers, or the public. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply Please upload a copy of your unofficial transcript with your application materials. To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.206": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Project Coordinator - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Project Coordinator School of Continuing Education Competition No. 26.08.206 Category Salary Closing Date Part-Time Non Recurring Term (less than 35 hours per week) MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $47,106 - $68,493 per annum (Based on 28 hours per week). The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Part-Time Non Recurring Term (less than 35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $47,106 - $68,493 per annum (Based on 28 hours per week). Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Project Coordinator for a part-time (0.8 FTE) 15-month, non-recurring term opportunity with the School of Continuing Education. The Project Coordinator is responsible for coordinating the planning, organization, and delivery of projects that advance the School of Continuing Education’s (SCE) strategic goals. Under the direction of the Senior Business Development Officer, the Project Coordinator translates established project goals and priorities into actionable project plans and ensures activities remain aligned with defined outcomes. You will manage project plans, schedules, budgets, and documentation, facilitating communication among internal and external stakeholders, and supporting quality assurance, reporting, and evaluation. By applying project management best practices, you will help ensure that projects are delivered on time, within scope and budget, and in alignment with institutional policies and stakeholder requirements. Where projects are grant-funded, the role also coordinates compliance, reporting, and financial accountability activities to ensure projects meet funding requirements and deliverables. Key responsibilities include: Coordinating activities, timelines, and roles with multiple stakeholders; Breaking down major deliverables into manageable components, integrating milestones into project schedules, and monitoring progress against agreed deadlines; Coordinating the people, materials, and services required to achieve project outcomes and program development goals; Tracking and reporting on budgeted spending, grants, and/or inventory to support accountability and transparency; Coordinating procurement of external services, consultants, SMEs, and other project resources in accordance with university processes; where applicable, ensuring alignment and compliance with funding agreements and guidelines; Organizing and facilitating meetings, preparing agendas, records decisions, and following up on action items; Managing communication protocols (e.g., shared calendars, resource repositories, process maps) to ensure clarity and accountability among internal and external stakeholders; Managing events, focus groups, and sector consultations; Preparing and maintaining accurate project documentation, including contracts, agreements, meeting minutes, records, and progress updates; Preparing status updates, briefing notes, presentations, updates, and final reports for leadership and stakeholders; and Collaborating and communicating effectively with all project stakeholders with an appropriate cadence. Skills You will have: Strong project coordination skills with a solid understanding of project management principles, methods, and techniques; The ability to navigate and coordinate multistakeholder projects; The ability to define and refine project requirements throughout the project lifecycle, ensuring clarity and alignment with outcomes; Demonstrated ability to problem-solve, assess situations, think critically, and apply sound judgment in making timely and informed recommendations; Strong collaboration and communication skills; Strong analytical and decision-making skills with keen attention to detail and accuracy; The ability to navigate sector-specific communications, spaces, and networks; The ability to develop trust by consistently displaying honesty, integrity, and ethical conduct in all interactions, fostering credibility, accountability, and strong working relationships with colleagues and stakeholders; The ability to identify, assess, and mitigate risks related to project scope, timelines, funding requirements, and deliverables; Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to articulate complex information, prepare reports, and tailor messaging to diverse audiences; Demonstrated self-motivation and initiative, effectively working independently while collaborating productively within a team environment to achieve shared goals and deliver results; Strong interpersonal, collaboration, and conflict resolution skills that enable positive and productive stakeholder relationships; Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to adapt to shifting priorities, manage multiple deadlines, and maintain focus under pressure; Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and collaboration platforms; and Experience using Asana, Hubspot, SIS and Outlook, Sharepoint and Teams would be considered an asset. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, or related field. A minimum of 3 years of project coordination experience, preferably in a post-secondary or public sector environment. Demonstrated experience coordinating projects with multiple stakeholders. Experience with budget tracking and reconciliation. Experience or knowledge of the transportation sector would be considered an asset. Experience working on multi-stakeholder projects would be considered an asset. Experience with grant-funded projects, compliance reporting, or government funding agreements would be considered an asset. Experience supporting program or curriculum development projects would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.209": {
      "title": "Recreation Assistant (Student Casual)",
      "description": "Recreation Assistant (Student Casual) - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Recreation Assistant (Student Casual) Sport and Wellness, Campus Services Competition No. 26.08.209 Category Salary Closing Date Student Casual (less than 35 hours per week) MSU Band A, Step 3: $18.754 per hour. September 10, 2026 Category Student Casual (less than 35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band A, Step 3: $18.754 per hour. Closing Date September 10, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking energetic and enthusiastic students to fill casual Recreation Assistant opportunities with the Sport and Wellness department. The Recreation Assistant will be the on-site leader of recreation leagues. Recreation offers 8 and 9-week leagues in both the Fall and Winter terms. Fall leagues take place from late September to early December, while Winter leagues run from late January to early April with statutory holidays and academic breaks off. Evening leagues run Monday through Thursday, and lunch leagues run Tuesdays and Wednesdays between 11:00am and 2:00pm. Key responsibilities include: Assisting in the marketing and delivery of recreation leagues and programs; Assisting with Sport and Wellness social media content creation and execution; Assisting with set-up and takedown of league supplies and equipment; Managing conflict by addressing disciplinary issues with participants; Assisting with the training, and mentoring of league staff and referees; Being the on-site coordinator for the end of season League Wrap-up and presenting prizing to winners; and Attending recreation training. Skills You will have: Knowledge of sports, including rules, format, rosters, and equipment set up; The ability to work effectively in a team, as well as independently; Strong interpersonal and communication including oral and written skills; Positive leadership qualities; Organizational skills with a high attention to detail; and The ability to multitask and manage time and schedules. Qualifications Standard First Aid certification. Experience in recreation and event management and leadership roles would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. The ability to lift and push equipment in excess of 50lbs (22 kg) during set-up and take-down tasks. The ability to work a minimum of 4 hours per week during league hours on weekday evenings and/or afternoons. May be required to work additional hours for special events and tournaments. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.200": {
      "title": "Security Services Agent",
      "description": "Security Services Agent - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Security Services Agent Campus Safety and Security Services Competition No. 26.08.200 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (38.5 hours per week) MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $64,769 - $95,741 per annum (Based on 38.5 hours per week). September 9, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (38.5 hours per week) Salary MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $64,769 - $95,741 per annum (Based on 38.5 hours per week). Closing Date September 9, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Security Services Agent for full-time continuing opportunity with our Campus Safety and Security Services department. You will exercise authority being licensed under the Security Services and Investigators Act of Alberta. Delivering services outlined in the university Security Services policy (D5040) and are responsible to work within applicable legislation, university policy and procedure, the Criminal Code, the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms, and all other provincial/federal legislation. You will work to diminish any risk to the safe learning environment on campus and to protect MacEwan's assets. You will be required to engage in community response and community problem solving initiatives. We may hire up to nine Security Services Agents. Key responsibilities include: Responding to alarms, issues with plant systems, emergency telephones and use CCTV (camera) systems; Providing information to staff, students, contractors, patrons, and visitors on request or proactively when noticing a person in need; Performing access control duties including but not limited to; door unlocks and lock-up, notifying and assisting with the removal of unauthorized individuals to leave the buildings, and perform building checks (interior) to ensure there are no intruders; Conducting investigations of reported incidents where there is a suspected breach of university policy; this may include taking statements, photographing scenes, gathering physical evidence, protecting a crime scene for police response, writing detailed notes, and entering all information into MacEwan's incident management software; Performing extensive interior, exterior, and licensed-area foot patrols, climbing stairs, handling potential physical confrontations; Conducting shift debriefs with the on-coming shift members to ensure effective communication is provided to alert shift activity or incidents that may require further attention/work or to make the on-coming shift members aware of activity or risks that may be expected; Assisting Parking Services and performing safe-walks within a two-block campus radius; Providing front counter service, log lost & found, writing reports, complying with FOIP policies; Ensuring all material handed over to external police agencies comply with university FOIP procedures and a completed law enforcement disclosure form is signed by the police and is on file/scanned in the report; Continually monitoring activity during the patrols on campus and leased property and apply the appropriate response to maintain a safe learning environment that may include enforcement of university policy, municipal legislation, limited authorized authority under provincial legislation, and arrest for trespassing or for criminal violations; Using the 10-codes and the phonetic alphabet to report all activities and requests over the radio system while on patrol or responding to a call for service; Responding to calls for medical assistance by providing first aid, maintaining the safety of the person, granting access for EMS/fire/police and supporting evacuations during emergencies; and Educating and mentoring the campus community on safety programs, prevention initiatives and security issues through informal engagement during patrols. Skills You will have: Working knowledge of Security practices and legislation covering authorities granted to the Security Agents; The ability to engage in a physically demanding role, required to be physically fit and participate in annual self-defense training and fitness testing; The aptitude to follow instructions and to read and interpret policy/legislation; Strong interpersonal skills to be able to maintain cooperative and professional relationships within the Security Services team; The expertise to use logic and reasoning when providing service to clients; The competency to quickly evaluate, prioritize, and deliver effective service; Strong report writing and verbal communication skills; The capability to quickly react to make critical decisions in threatening or emergency situations and to be able to multi-task under pressure; and The proficiency to use FM radio communication effectively using 10-code and the phonetic alphabet. Qualifications A graduate of a Security Services course recognized by the Government of Alberta that complies with licensing requirements for security services workers in the Province of Alberta. Current Standard First Aid certificate. Completion of post-secondary education in a related field such as Police and Investigations or a similar discipline is considered an asset. ICS 100 is considered an asset. Prior experience in a post-secondary institution is an asset. Minimum two years' experience as a licensed security services worker or equivalent customer service experience with completion of a Police Studies/Investigation Studies diploma will be considered. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position can only be held by a person licensed under the Security Services and Investigators Act by the Province of Alberta. Any cancellation/removal or expiry of that license would be cause for termination. The successful incumbent will be required to obtain a Police Record Check, including a Vulnerable Sector Check. The successful incumbent will be required to provide a valid driver’s abstract. This position requires shift work and availability 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.07.170": {
      "title": "Senior Development Officer",
      "description": "Senior Development Officer - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Senior Development Officer Advancement, University Relations Competition No. 26.07.170 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Non-Recurring Term (35 hours per week) & Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). A review of applications will begin on August 5, 2026 and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Non-Recurring Term (35 hours per week) & Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date A review of applications will begin on August 5, 2026 and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking 2 Senior Development Officers for 1 full-time, 12-month non-recurring term and 1 full-time continuing opportunity with our Advancement department. Reporting to the Director, Development, the Senior Development Officer (SDO) develops and leads strategic fundraising initiatives that inspire philanthropic investment in MacEwan University's priorities. You will manage a portfolio of significant donor relationships and philanthropic opportunities and develop sophisticated donor cultivation and engagement strategies to secure transformational philanthropic support. In this role, you will serve as a strategic relationship manager by identifying opportunities to engage institutional leaders and partners in support of donor relationships and fundraising initiatives. You will develop and recommend strategies to involve senior University representatives, including the President, Vice-President University Relations, Deans, faculty, volunteers, and other stakeholders, with approaches implemented in collaboration with Advancement leadership. You will also contribute to campaign fundraising priorities and strategic initiatives while fostering a collaborative, innovative, and high-performing Advancement culture. If you are passionate about philanthropy and committed to helping donors create meaningful impact through charitable giving, this is the opportunity for you. Key responsibilities include: Managing a portfolio of major gift prospects and donors involving significant philanthropic opportunities, multiple stakeholders, complex gift arrangements, and strategic institutional priorities using the University's prospect management process; Achieving fundraising objectives by leading strategic fundraising initiatives, advancing complex donor relationships, and securing philanthropic support for assigned institutional priorities; Developing strategies and recommending appropriate opportunities to engage senior University leaders with engagement approaches approved in collaboration with Advancement leadership; Building and maintaining trusted partnerships with individuals, corporations, foundations, and community partners capable of making significant philanthropic investments across the University; Developing comprehensive fundraising strategies, coordinating donor engagement activities and leading creative engagement opportunities that connect donor interests with institutional priorities and deepen donor relationships; Evaluating donor readiness and determining appropriate cultivation and solicitation approaches based on donor interests, giving capacity, and engagement history; Negotiating gift opportunities involving restricted gifts, endowments, naming opportunities, multi-year commitments, and other arrangements requiring collaboration across the University; Supporting institutional fundraising priorities as the fundraiser lead, and contributing to executive briefings, donor strategies, special initiatives, campaign planning, and fundraising priorities; Serving as the primary relationship manager for donors within the assigned portfolio; Collaborating with and facilitating between donors and internal stakeholders to ensure alignment between donor interests and University priorities; Researching and analyzing prospective donor interests, philanthropic trends, and funding opportunities, capacity, and alignment with university priorities; Maintaining accurate records and portfolio strategies within Raiser's Edge; and Contributing to building a high-performing fundraising culture characterized by collaboration, accountability, innovation, continuous learning, and shared success. Skills You will have: Success building, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding long-term relationships with donors, alumni, corporations, foundations, and community partners; Exceptional interpersonal, networking, influencing, and relationship management skills with the ability to establish credibility and trust with diverse stakeholders; Excellent written, verbal, presentation, and proposal development skills; Strong strategic thinking, analytical, negotiation, and problem-solving abilities; The ability to develop and implement sophisticated fundraising strategies that align donor interests with institutional priorities and campaign objectives; Political acuity, sound judgment, professionalism, and discretion when working with confidential information and senior institutional representatives; Strong collaboration skills with the ability to work effectively across academic and administrative units and recognize that successful fundraising is achieved through coordinated institutional engagement; The ability to inspire confidence and build authentic relationships with donors, volunteers, colleagues, and University leadership; Initiative, resilience, adaptability, accountability, and sound judgment in a dynamic fundraising environment; Positive, optimistic, and solutions-oriented approach to relationship building and fundraising; Strong organizational and planning skills with the ability to manage a complex donor portfolio and multiple priorities in a results-oriented environment; Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and donor relationship management systems, including Raiser's Edge; and A high degree of integrity and commitment to ethical fundraising practices and exceptional donor experiences. Qualifications A minimum of an undergraduate degree in business, communications, public relations, marketing, or a related field. A minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible experience managing major gift fundraising, strategic donor relationships, advancement, business development, or complex external partnerships, including demonstrated success securing significant philanthropic investments. Professional affiliation with organizations such as the Association of Fundraising Professionals (AFP), Canadian Association of Gift Planners (CAGP), or the Canadian Council for the Advancement of Education (CCAE) would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth Additional benefits vary by appointment type. Continuing employees have participation in the Local Authorities Pension Plan (LAPP). How to Apply Please indicate in your cover letter if you are interested in applying for the term position or the continuing position. To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.202": {
      "title": "Specialist, Admission Evaluation",
      "description": "Specialist, Admission Evaluation - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Specialist, Admission Evaluation Office of the University Registrar Competition No. 26.08.202 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 17, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 17, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Specialist, Admission Evaluation for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Office of the University Registrar. The Specialist, Admission Evaluation plays a pivotal role in supporting the student lifecycle by managing comprehensive admissions processes with a strong emphasis on accuracy, consistency, transparency, and a student-centered approach. You will be responsible for evaluating applications and making informed admissions decisions for domestic, international, and transfer applicants. This role requires ensuring that all decisions align with institutional policies and procedures, Faculty- or School-specific admission criteria, and applicable provincial privacy legislation. A thorough understanding of these frameworks is essential to ensuring that admissions decisions are consistent, equitable, and compliant. You will also provide timely, accurate, and empathetic guidance to applicants, agents, faculty, and staff regarding admission and transfer credit policies and procedures. Through clear communication and supportive service, this role helps shape a positive and informed student experience, building trust and confidence in MacEwan’s admissions processes from first contact through to enrolment. Key responsibilities include: Evaluating and interpreting domestic and international secondary and post-secondary academic credentials to determine admissibility, requiring in-depth knowledge of Canadian provincial/territorial and global education systems, grading scales, grade conversions, and higher education accreditation; Applying general and program specific admission requirements, including Faculty- or School-specific criteria and processes; Authenticating and verifying transcripts, credentials, English language proficiency, and other non-standard academic documents; Generating admission letters for applicants at various stages of the admission process, ensuring timely and accurate communication to support a smooth applicant experience; Providing clear, empathetic guidance to applicants, students, recruiters, academic advisors, and other university stakeholders on admission and transfer credit statuses, policies, processes, program and course requirements, fees and withdrawals; Updating the student information system with relevant data and decisions to ensure applicants can view accurate, up-to-date statuses and information online; Maintaining application statuses by updating actions/action reasons and checklist items to reflect requirements and progress; and Building and maintaining transfer of articulation rules in the student information system. Skills You will have: A customer service-oriented approach with a commitment to service excellence; The ability to understand, interpret, and apply diverse and complex Canadian and International educational systems against established admission and transfer credit criteria across multiple faculties and programs; The ability to understand, interpret, and apply departmental policies and procedures; Familiarity with transfer credit assessment practices, including course evaluation and articulation; Knowledge of ATIA and POPA; Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to explain complex information clearly and professionally; Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to operate with a high degree of tact, diplomacy, professionalism, and sensitivity; Strong analytical, problem-solving, decision-making, critical thinking, and conflict resolution skills; A self-motivated attitude with excellent organizational and time management skills, along with keen attention to detail and accuracy; The ability to remain calm and professional in challenging, fast-paced circumstances; A proven ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and adapt to shifting priorities in a fast-paced and dynamic work environment; The ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment; Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, SharePoint, Google, and in using student information systems like PeopleSoft or related applications; and Dedication to providing excellent student-focused service. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor's degree in Business, Education, Administration, or related field. A minimum of 2 years of experience in a related role, such as admissions, enrolment management, credential evaluation, program evaluation, or a related administrative environment. Experience with evaluating Canadian or international education to determine admission eligibility and transfer credit would be considered an asset. Experience with PeopleSoft - Campus Solutions would be considered an asset. Proficiency in a second language would also be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
